d-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(2,2)$ and ${B}^{′}(-5,7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159797/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159797"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-77709"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/fa8ce497e80e941730cebb8528b09725930fcb31c839ac0020ce7cf9f0a39b58.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}},$ the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(-3,6)$ and ${B}^{′}(5,-3),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/26d4f8e966818e27a0858da0aa8757cf71ebbd1ef0e0544a2b8a126810252def.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-77699/selection/b98d963b7d20269e7b3732bc3f6651324245c5c93fc0d372108cb6d1dbf4ba83" :answer/id #uuid "fde7f563-d6f3-558b-a9ec-9923b59bc4d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,1)$ and $(2,-3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77699/selection/c268ad37488782d0323c9a7e1b6e3d44b1ecc5f859ec963815cb3a7b210a1d32" :answer/id #uuid "86aa7f09-d514-5b65-a57d-f7bed8ea8137" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,1)$ and $(1,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77699/selection/5d9a96c3d4f140506361a851ab363e50c1f29b01bfdc611b5bfddc99c2cc74f7" :answer/id #uuid "c526bf96-1a73-5b6f-a2af-31f3ad44b37c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-1)$ and $(1,-3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77699/selection/5a3ba429344b8ed98183034a2f4d355bed477a3a8f419de6dbea63001be6a3c4" :answer/id #uuid "2971cfd8-8236-504b-8914-d6c0ad4c36db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,1)$ and $(1,-3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77699/selection/b34acda96791fb39087365739da92386b04e4ac4ccafcf04aa73c87d28294bf3" :answer/id #uuid "879b2f49-c73b-532f-8e10-1e264f80f623" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-3,1)$ and $(1,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77699/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c7987b-9a97-5476-976b-3d88ffc5c95d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77699/selection/5a3ba429344b8ed98183034a2f4d355bed477a3a8f419de6dbea63001be6a3c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-77699/selection/b98d963b7d20269e7b3732bc3f6651324245c5c93fc0d372108cb6d1dbf4ba83" "q-77699/selection/c268ad37488782d0323c9a7e1b6e3d44b1ecc5f859ec963815cb3a7b210a1d32" "q-77699/selection/5d9a96c3d4f140506361a851ab363e50c1f29b01bfdc611b5bfddc99c2cc74f7" "q-77699/selection/5a3ba429344b8ed98183034a2f4d355bed477a3a8f419de6dbea63001be6a3c4" "q-77699/selection/b34acda96791fb39087365739da92386b04e4ac4ccafcf04aa73c87d28294bf3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77699" :question/id #uuid "19042bce-c915-5186-a2d2-3f28f8435edc" :question/math-academy-id "q-77699" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ has endpoints at $A(2,3)$ and $B(1,-2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(2,1)$ and ${B}^{′}(1,-3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-77699/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-282616/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ee165f41-3318-5eb2-9b32-30d70fe