alidate]} {:db/id "q-281567" :question/id #uuid "39092da6-a6f3-5ce1-9ece-f9716d31fa11" :question/math-academy-id "q-281567" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $GHI$ has vertices at $G(5,5),\\,H(-1,-4),$ and $I(3,5).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{G}^{′}{H}^{′}{I}^{′}$, the image of $△GHI$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${G}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{H}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{I}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $△GHI$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $GHI:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 15 & -17 \\\\ 25 & -14 & 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{G}^{′}{H}^{′}{I}^{′}$ are ${G}^{′}(-15,25),$\n${H}^{′}(15,-14),$ ${I}^{′}(-17,21).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-281567/field-1" "q-281567/field-2" "q-281567/field-3" "q-281567/field-4" "q-281567/field-5" "q-281567/field-6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281567"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12033/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "6f3436aa-bc6f-5420-90bf-14ca61e1eb69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12033/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "bd6d2dc2-589b-539f-ad79-4d4b1963b84f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12033/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "c04776d6-80c4-5774-b0fe-c35c114e64a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12033/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "183ad56d-58ec-5cde-90c9-3d1d3e3d2e70" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12033/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "6cb10166-6de0-58ae-9c5a-1768164fafe5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12033/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "49ae9de8-3f45-5dd4-9da7-b22a8a5e5c02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12033/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-12033/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-12033/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-12033/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-12033/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-12033/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12033" :question/id #uuid "afcd3422-c3b2-56a7-a256-45fffe148caa" :question/math-academy-id "q-12033" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,1),(3,3),$ and $(5,-2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(5,-2)$\n- $(-2,-5)$\n- $(3,12)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-2,-5),(3,12),(5,13).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-12033/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12033"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-159801"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/d9ec98b03009d1023668aa12de88ed5515f0ea6df058d1b5d17804bf42082c5c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(6,4),(1,-6),(-3,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/4c43c4c793924d4fde32b59c93b7a19be0109a389b126665868396b4c06d721e.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-8125/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "cbc35c5f-3d8d-58b0-85f3-a92064e9e3ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8125/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "860351fd-7c98-547d-af55-54ce581a13ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8125/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "a8c0b201-00ef-5c8d-8c2c-43129921e0ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8125/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "5e379d27-0003-5685-98b5-f1dd37cd058f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8125/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "b2e55b47-b975-5c49-ab3b-e08da78de8dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8125/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "479ba3aa-a8ec-575e-8b63-d8b9a8188ce5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8125/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-8125/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-8125/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-8125/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-8125/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-8125/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8125" :question/id #uuid "e2444a5c-7bef-56b8-ad82-b35e0384de25" :question/math-academy-id "q-8125" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-3,0),(3,0),$ and $(0,-3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(21,0)$\n- $(3,0)$\n- $(-21,0)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-21,0),(21,0),(0,3).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8125/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8125"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8097"] :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,1),(2,3),$ and $(5,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(4,-1)$\n- $(17,-3)$\n- $(10,-1)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(4,-1),(17,-3),(10,-1).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6682"] :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/73f0065d4d4768a2c3432559702c2db28fefd050194a5bcdfe44ac3e0b736c82.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{AB}$ is shown below. Find $\\overline{A'B'},$ the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/2e22400d15abc81150d6d18de591549e81a46bd16ab9e95f10f86bae2125b490.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overline{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/fe82a0c8616e43c9d8db0b2892a145fcabf4cfa17bd3d4e033a1349cd25921ee.png)\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are $A'(1,3)$ and $B'(1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/472f8e712f7d695d5ab3593dafbcc0309feb1a6ac80e9e29c4893dc651d20cf7.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5447"] :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/10c3819b661a1831f747c949089a9133b4d0df7b07a66efe588c12bab469136e.png)\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown below. Find $\\triangle A'B'C',$ the image of $\\triangle ABC$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/4986bd2dab6b455c0d5e41909377c433d761bf7270364d3e2596e6db7f23981b.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $\\triangle ABC\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/0cd1d198e714f41437302bdf21c17979409a533d3055b5b4dc519855d6fc8efb.png)\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $\\triangle A'B'C'$ are $(-3,-4), (0,0), (1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/e8a14ffbaab4597a2a4a7c9a6bad61dabbc4970fc22c3ed2eb28b2594a670938.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
